  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilience Fund GI-TOC:  Helping communities turn the tide against criminal governance through the Resilience Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Fund will aim to reduce violence and foster peaceful societies by:
A. building resilience to criminal governance in local communities through identifying and empowering a growing and global network of community-based individuals and initiatives.
B.  driving catalytic growth of resilience around the world, as lessons are shared through the Fund&apos;s networks, and as connections are made between different communities, and as best practices are published and disseminated.

The target groups will primarily be located in Least Developed Countries (LDCs) and will all be based in communities facing acute organized crime related problems, and where beneficiaries able to have an impact are identified by the Resilience Fund and wider GI-TOC team.</narrative>
  </description>
